        "commit_message": "Fixes https://github.com/cython/cython/issues/8048\n\nWith `CYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE`, the create function now raises `ImportError`\nif the module already exists in this interpreter, instead of returning it.\nCPython resets `md_state` on the module that create returns,\nso returning the live module wiped its state and the process crashed later.\nThe first module keeps working.\n\nBuilds without module state are unchanged. There the globals don't live in `md_state`,\nso returning the existing module works, and `reimport_from_package` relies on it\nwhen it imports the same module under a second name.\n\nTests:\n- New `tests/run/reimport_module_state.srctree`. It fails on master: the\n  second import succeeds, and calling into the module after that\n  segfaults. It passes with this change.\n- Importing the same module under a second name (`pkg.demo`, then `demo`\n  from inside `pkg`) segfaults on master and now raises the same\n  `ImportError`.\n- The existing reimport and subinterpreter tests still pass on 3.9,\n  3.12, 3.14, 3.14t, and 3.14 with `--limited-api`.",
        "commit_title": "Raise ImportError when a module with module state is imported again (GH-8057)",
