    "body": "Fixes #8048\n\nWith `CYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE`, the create function now raises `ImportError` if the module already exists in this interpreter, instead of returning it. CPython resets `md_state` on the module that create returns, so returning the live module wiped its state and the process crashed later. The first module keeps working.\n\nBuilds without module state are unchanged. There the globals don't live in `md_state`, so returning the existing module works, and `reimport_from_package` relies on it when it imports the same module under a second name.\n\nTests:\n- New `tests/run/reimport_module_state.srctree`. It fails on master: the second import succeeds, and calling into the module after that segfaults. It passes with this change.\n- Importing the same module under a second name (`pkg.demo`, then `demo` from inside `pkg`) segfaults on master and now raises the same `ImportError`.\n- The existing reimport and subinterpreter tests still pass on 3.9, 3.12, 3.14, 3.14t, and 3.14 with `--limited-api`.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-18T02:57:34Z",
